    {
      "version": "1.1.0",
      "tag": "coding-agents-v1.1.0",
      "released": "2026-11-25T07:08:16Z",
      "notes": "- **Claude Limits** and **Codex Limits** keys (5-hour, weekly and, for Claude, Fable gauges), replacing the AI Stats plugin.\n- No more rate limiting: the numbers come from Claude Code's status line and Codex's session logs, with no network calls. The providers' usage endpoints are only a fallback when those numbers are over 15 minutes old, at most once per 10 minutes, with `Retry-After` and a growing back-off kept across restarts; the last good numbers stay on the key meanwhile.\n- Setup can connect Claude Code's status line for this (on by default). A status line you already have keeps working and is restored when you untick it.",
      "meta": {
        "dir": "coding-agents",
        "version": "1.1.0",
        "name": "Coding Agents",
        "summary": "Claude Code and Codex session status; approve or deny requests from a key.",
